   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Substituting \\( x = 1 \\) and \\( f(1) = -4 \\) into the relation gives \\( f^{\\prime}(1) = 6 \\).",
         "mathjson": 6,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99027",
         "rule_named": "evaluate the relation"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule, \\( f^{\\prime\\prime}(x) = -f(x) - x f^{\\prime}(x) \\), so \\( f^{\\prime\\prime}(1) = -2 \\).",
         "mathjson": -2,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99022",
         "rule_named": "product rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Differentiating again, \\( f^{\\prime\\prime\\prime}(x) = -2 f^{\\prime}(x) - x f^{\\prime\\prime}(x) \\), so \\( f^{\\prime\\prime\\prime}(1) = -10 \\).",
         "mathjson": -10,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99027",
         "rule_named": "product rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Dividing each value by the matching factorial, the polynomial is \\( -4 + 6 \\left(x - 1\\right) - \\left(x - 1\\right)^{2} - \\frac{5}{3} \\left(x - 1\\right)^{3} \\).",
